## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React + Vite project.

### Changes Made

**1. Installed Package**
   - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 to dependencies
   - Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json`

**2. Modified Files**
   - `src/App.jsx`: 
     - Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
     - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the root level of the App component (just before the closing div)

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (retrieved from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), the installation was done according to React/Vite framework-specific instructions:

1. Used the `/react` import path as specified for React applications
2. Placed the component at the root level of the application for proper tracking
3. The SpeedInsights component is self-contained and will automatically collect performance metrics once deployed to Vercel

### Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ No new linting errors introduced (pre-existing errors remain unchanged)
- ✅ Package installation completed without issues
- ✅ Lock file updated correctly

### Next Steps

Once this code is deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance data
2. Data will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section
3. The Speed Insights script will be automatically injected at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` routes
4. Performance metrics will appear in the dashboard after several days of visitor traffic

### Notes

- The implementation preserves all existing code structure and functionality
- No breaking changes were introduced
- The SpeedInsights component is lightweight and non-blocking
